
### Script to Retrain TSplice and MTSplice models on COMPASS ###
INPUTS:
--mtsplice_model_number
    model number to load if testing loaded weights 
--mmsplice_model_number
    retrained MMSplice model number for combining with MTSplice
--load_data
    If True, will load splits from mtsplice_data_dir and
    tsplice_data_dir 
--load_ascot_data
    If True, will load ascot data from ascot_data_dir and
    add it to the tsplice data (not MTSplice since it doesn't
    predict variant effects) 
--ascot_data_dir
    Data containing ASCOT dataset used to train the original TSplice
    model. It should already be separated into train, val, test
    in the same way as the original paper. 
--tsplice_data_dir
    Tsplice cell type delta logit data (cell - mean cell)
    and one hot encoded sequences already split into train/val/test
--mtsplice_data_dir 
    MTsplice variant delta logit data 
    by cell (variant cell - reference cell)
    and one hot encoded sequences already split into train/val/test
--output_models_dir
    Where to save and load .hdf5 or .keras model weights from.
--output_figures_dir
    Directory denoting where to save figures to.
--baseline_mmsplice_path
    path containing original MMSplice cloned GitHub 
--test_loaded_weights
    If True, will try to load weights using mtsplice_model_number
    and perform predictions on it.
--tsplice_n_epochs
    epochs to train tsplice for
--tsplice_loss
    either "mse" or "huber". A string containing which loss
    function to use.
--tsplice_learning_rate
    float representing the tsplice learning rate,
    if not hyperparameter tuning.
--tsplice_batch_size
    batch size to use for tsplice training.
--tsplice_cell_weights
    relative cell weights, used to prioritize predictions
    for certain cell types
--tsplice_early_stop
    indicate whether to stop the tsplice hyperband at the optimal
    val loss or not.
--tsplice_patience
    patience for early stopping .
--mtsplice_n_epochs
    epochs to train mtsplice for.
--mtsplice_loss
    either "mse" or "huber". A string containing which loss
    function to use.
--mtsplice_learning_rate
    float representing the mtsplice learning rate,
    if not hyperparameter tuning.
--mtsplice_batch_size
    batch size to use for mtsplice training.
--mtsplice_cell_weights
    relative cell weights, used to prioritize predictions
    for certain cell types.
--mtsplice_early_stop 
    indicate whether to stop the tsplice hyperband at the optimal
    val loss or not.
--mtsplice_patience
    patience for mtsplice hyperband.
--gpu_memory
    can lower to avoid OOM errors when predicting
    or training MTSplice (i.e. 4 ensemble + MMSplice).
--weight_initializer
    experimental value to see if weight reinitialization helps .
--hyperparameter_tune
    If true, will perform hyperband rather than regular fit.
--hyperband_n_epochs
--hyperband_max_n_epochs
--hyperband_patience
--hyperband_retrain_n_epochs
    After hyperband, the number of epochs to retrain
    the best hyperparameter set for.
--hyperband_retrain_patience
--hyperband_lr_bounds
    comma-separated two value input
    denoting the minimum and maximum learning rate to 
    optimize for with hyperband.
--freeze_mmsplice_layers
    If True, will freeze MMSplice layers during the 
    full MTSplice retraining.
--tsplice_natural_scale
    If True, will produce predictions for the actual 
    cell logits rather than delta logits.
--tsplice_output_cell_scale
    explicitly tell model to train on either
    "logit", "dlogit", "psi" or "dpsi" scales.
--nan_mask_strategy
    How to handle missing values in train.
    Default is zero-inpute.
--output_plot_scale
    Comma-separated input displaying which scale
    to produce plots for (generally should de "dlogit").
    options: "logit", "dlogit", "psi" or "dpsi".
--merged_data_path
    If make data, full path to where to get 
    the merged (MMSplice) data from.
--all_samples_data_path
    If make data, full path to where to get 
    the all samples (i.e. with missing refs) data from.
--mmsplice_data_dir
    If make data, full path to where to get 
    mmsplice data from.
--slurm_job_id
    passed in automatically by the script if using sbatch.
    Otherwise, it should be None.
--make_data
    Not currently implemented, should use the make_mtsplice_data_splits.sh
    script to make the data instead.
--debug
    Set default values for all parameters and allow breakpoints
    for debugging.
--help
    Display this message.
